Sodium, https://github.com/CaffeineMC/sodium (0.9.2 for Minecraft 26.3)
Copyright the Sodium contributors
PolyForm Shield License 1.0.0
  src/main/java/io/github/hecbatista/metalshaders/sodium/LuxiumChunkVertex.java writes
  Sodium's compact chunk vertex words the same way as Sodium's CompactChunkVertex (position
  quantisation and interleaving, texture shrink bit, light + 8, light/material/section word),
  so Sodium's own shader can still read our mesh. glsl/ProgramTranslator.java's terrain
  header decodes that vertex as Sodium's shaders/include/chunk_vertex.glsl and
  blocks/block_layer_opaque.vsh do, and declares Sodium's u_Globals block and push-constant
  layout so the pack's program binds to what Sodium already sets. These are re-written
  short formulas needed to interoperate with Sodium's data format; no Sodium file is shipped.
